“The statutes governing a political organisation
must especially indicate the following:
1º its full name ;
2º its objectives;
3º its insignia;
4º its organs and their structure including the
organ in charge of discipline and
10
settlement of disputes and the organ in
charge of audit;
5º its head office which must be in Rwanda;
6º members of its organs, modalities for their
election and replacement, their term of
office and their responsibilities;
7º requirements for membership, procedures
for resignation and reasons for dismissal of
members;
8º the legal representatives of a political
organisation;
9º provisions related to the property;
10º provisions relating to the amendments of
its statutes or its dissolution;
11º allocation of its assets in case of its
dissolution”.

“The property of the National Consultative Forum
of Political Organisations comes from the
following sources:
1º subsidies and grants from Government
and partners;
2º donations;
3º bequests;
4º loans granted to the National Consultative
Forum of Political Organisations;
5º proceeds from the activities of the
National Consultative Forum of Political
Organisations;
